{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/httpdestinations"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"externalID":"HTTPDestinations","roleHeading":"Framework","symbolKind":"module","modules":[{"name":"HTTPDestinations"}],"title":"HTTPDestinations","role":"collection"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" is a destination that posts each batch it receives as the requests its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":" splits it into: one request for an endpoint without limits. Each body is whatever"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the encoder writes for its records, so events need no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance and the wire format is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"yours. It sends with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URLSession"},{"type":"text","text":" through"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/URLSessionTransport"},{"type":"text","text":" by default, or through any "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransport"},{"type":"text","text":" you pass."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A send that gets no response, or a 5xx, 408 or 429 status, is sent again after the next wait of its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":": nominally 1 second, doubling up to 60 seconds, unless you pass another. So"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is one answered with a status the encoder lists in "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder\/transientStatuses","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", which every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"encoder declares: empty for most servers, or each other failure its vendor answers to a request"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"worth sending again, such as Aptabase’s 418 for a slow upload."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each wait has full jitter by default: a random wait shorter than the nominal one, so apps refused"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"at the same moment retry at different moments. Pass "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff\/Jitter-swift.enum\/none","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nominal waits. In tests, pass a seeded generator as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"randomNumberGenerator:"},{"type":"text","text":" for jittered waits"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that repeat from one run to the next, as long as one request retries at a time: copies of a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"destination retrying at once share the generator’s draws in the order they ask for them. Never"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"seed it in production, where every device would then wait the same, which defeats the jitter. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"destination takes the next batch only once this one is delivered or dropped, so a tracker’s store"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"keeps the batch’s records until then. A batch the endpoint answers with any other status, whose"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"request can never be sent, or that the encoder can’t encode is dropped, logged and reported on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/dropReports","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" as an "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDropReport","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", as is each record the encoder leaves out"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of its requests. So is a request still undelivered at its "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/EncodedRequest\/deadline","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", which an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"encoder sets for a vendor that misdates or ignores old events: the destination checks it on its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"now:"},{"type":"text","text":" clock before every attempt and sends nothing more once it has passed."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The tracing instrument injects the trace context of each request’s first record into its header"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fields, and "},{"code":"Content-Type","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is always the encoder’s."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reach for this module to send to a server whose format you write yourself. For TraffluentCollector’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"format, give the destination a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CollectorBatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CollectorEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":"); for PostHog,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"make it with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination.postHog(projectToken:host:plan:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PostHogEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":"); for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Amplitude, with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination.amplitude(apiKey:region:plan:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AmplitudeEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":"); for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Mixpanel, with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination.mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MixpanelEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":");"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for Segment, RudderStack or Customer.io Data Pipelines, with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination.segment(writeKey:region:plan:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"rudderStack(writeKey:dataPlane:plan:)"},{"type":"text","text":" or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"customerIO(apiKey:region:plan:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SegmentSpecEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":"); for Google Analytics 4, from a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"server, with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination.googleAnalytics(measurementID:apiSecret:region:plan:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (module"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GoogleAnalyticsEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":"); for Snowplow, with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination.snowplow(collector:vendor:appID:plan:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SnowplowEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":"); for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"TelemetryDeck, with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination.telemetryDeck(appID:namespace:testMode:plan:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (module"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TelemetryDeckEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":"); for Matomo, with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination.matomo(url:siteID:dimensions:category:plan:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MatomoEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":"); for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Heap, with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination.heap(appID:region:plan:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HeapEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":"); for Aptabase, with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination.aptabase(appKey:host:isDebug:plan:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AptabaseEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":"). To read events"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"inside the app or in a test, use"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"InMemoryDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Destinations"},{"type":"text","text":") instead."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import HTTPDestinations","","struct PlansEncoder: BatchEncoder {","    static let transientStatuses: Set<TransientStatus> = []","","    func requests(for batch: [EventRecord]) -> BatchRequests<Never> {","        let plans = batch.compactMap { ($0.event as? SignedUp)?.plan }","        let body = EncodedBatch(body: Data(plans.joined(separator: \"\\n\").utf8), contentType: \"text\/plain\")","        return BatchRequests(requests: [EncodedRequest(body: body, recordIDs: batch.map(\\.id))], skippedRecords: [])","    }","}","","let server = HTTPDestination(","    endpoint: endpointURL,","    headerFields: [.authorization: \"Bearer \\(token)\"],","    encoder: PlansEncoder(),","    backoff: try ExponentialBackoff(initialDelay: .seconds(2), maximumDelay: .seconds(120)))","let drops = server.dropReports","let watching = Task {","    for await drop in drops {","        print(\"Dropped a batch: \\(drop)\")","    }","}","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: server)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The guide ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","isActive":true},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers this destination beside the others, and what a delivery does while a batch is retried.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Sending-batches","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDropReport"],"title":"Sending batches"},{"anchor":"Encoding-a-batch","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/EncodedBatch"],"title":"Encoding a batch"},{"anchor":"Splitting-a-batch-into-requests","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchRequests","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/EncodedRequest","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/SkippedRecord"],"title":"Splitting a batch into requests"},{"anchor":"Retrying-a-vendors-own-statuses","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/TransientStatus","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/InvalidTransientStatus"],"title":"Retrying a vendor’s own statuses"},{"anchor":"Waiting-between-attempts","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/InvalidBackoff","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/NonPositiveRetry"],"title":"Wai